{"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenUSD in Swift is currently evolving and may change in the future. Here are some key features currently supported:"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Reference-types-in-Swift","text":"Reference types in Swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"UsdStage and SdfLayer are imported as classes in Swift and behave like classes written in Swift. When Swift passes a raw pointer to UsdStage or SdfLayer, Swift automatically increments or decrements the underlying reference count as needed, allowing Swift or C++ to influence the lifetime of the same UsdStage or SdfLayer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func makeTempStage() -> pxr.UsdStage {","    return Overlay.Dereference(pxr.UsdStage.CreateNew(\"\/tmp\/myStage.usda\", .LoadAll))","}","","func defineXform(_ stage: pxr.UsdStage, _ path: pxr.SdfPath) {","    stage.DefinePrim(path, .UsdGeomTokens.Xform)","}","","let stage = makeTempStage()","defineXform(stage, \"\/hello\")","let layer = Overlay.Dereference(stage.GetRootLayer())","layer.Save(false)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/WhatIsAForeignReferenceType"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/ForeignReferenceTypesAndSmartPointers"},{"type":"text","text":" for more information."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"warning","name":"Warning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When working in Swift, do not use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfRefPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfWeakPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" to dereference 